Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: publish NPU RX buffer before returning ownership

Clearing ctrl makes a recycled descriptor available to the NPU. Do not
clear it with memset before the replacement DMA address is installed.
Order all descriptor fields before the final ownership store, including
when the shared refill function is called from NAPI or queue reset.

Based on the RX ownership analysis published by NoTengoBattery:
https://forum.openwrt.org/t/quantum-fiber-w1700k-support/222776/3890

--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -32,8 +32,12 @@
 		page = virt_to_head_page(e->buf);
 		e->dma_addr[0] = page_pool_get_dma_addr(page) + offset;
 
-		memset(&desc[q->head], 0, sizeof(*desc));
+		desc[q->head].info = 0;
+		desc[q->head].data = 0;
 		desc[q->head].addr = e->dma_addr[0];
+		desc[q->head].rsv = 0;
+		dma_wmb();
+		WRITE_ONCE(desc[q->head].ctrl, 0);
 
 		q->head = (q->head + 1) % q->ndesc;
 		q->queued++;
